# PPMI is controlled-access. Nothing that identifies a participant, and nothing from which
# a participant-level record could be reconstructed, belongs in a public repository. The
# rules below are deliberately blunt: they block whole directories and then let back in only
# what has been checked by hand.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- raw and processed data --
# The raw download lives outside this folder and is never copied in. The processed parquets
# are one row per participant and are rebuilt by the pipeline from the raw tables.
04_Dados_processados/
01_Dados_Brutos/
*.parquet
*.pkl

# ------------------------------------------------- individual-level derived result files --
# Five tables under 03_Resultados carry PATNO and one row per participant. They are inputs
# to later scripts, not results anyone needs to read, and every one is regenerated by a
# script in the pipeline: 27_treatments_at_time_zero.py, 31_amantadine_handling.py,
# 32_internal_performance.py, 37_eligibility_sensitivity.py and 51_outcome_anchoring.py
# respectively.
#
# Each pattern must be alone on its line. A '#' opens a comment only at the start of a
# line, so a note written after a pattern becomes part of the pattern, and the rule then
# matches nothing. That mistake was in this file until it was caught by a dry run, and it
# would have published all five.
03_Resultados/Tabelas/tab27_treatments_per_patient.csv
03_Resultados/Tabelas/tab31_masking_candidates.csv
03_Resultados/Tabelas/tab32_out_of_fold_linear_predictor.csv
03_Resultados/Tabelas/tab37_excluded_participants.csv
03_Resultados/Tabelas/tab51_anchoring_measurements.csv

# ------------------------------------------------------------- unpublished written work --
00_Manuscrito/
01_Notas_de_trabalho/
06_Auditoria/
*.docx

# The project handover note and the assistant briefing. Internal working documents: the
# handover records audit findings not yet in the manuscript, the list of pending
# corrections to the current draft, and the internal reasoning behind study decisions.
# None of that belongs in a public code repository.
CONTEXTO.md
PROMPT_PARA_CLAUDE_CODE.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- local --
# Editor backups. A stale copy of a script sitting beside the real one is worse than no
# copy at all, because a reader cannot tell which one produced the results.
*.bak
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
